// #2830 (ADR-0096): `Option` is the ONE exemption from constructor
// qualification, and it is an exemption by ABSENCE rather than by policy --
// `Option::Some` resolves to nothing at all.
//
// Measured 2026-09-18 across every shape ADR-0096 names: a local enum, a type
// alias, an imported enum (plain and aliased) and the WIT-local
// `@vibe/wit_runtime` `Result` all accept BOTH the bare and the qualified
// spelling, in expressions and in patterns. `Option` accepts only the bare
// one. So the exemption set is exactly `{ Option }`, and the issue's warning
// holds: the WIT-local `Result` is not in it.
//
// This fixture is why that sentence in the cheatsheet can be trusted. Without
// it the exemption is prose, and prose about a name that resolves to nothing
// is exactly the kind that rots.
fn main() -> Int {
  match Option::Some(5) {
    Some(v) => v,
    None => 0
  }
}
